{
  "title": "Imports without a page show fetch_html as pending forever on the job status page",
  "description": "JobPlan::import() (server/src/scraping/plan.rs) always starts with fetch_html, but imports that have no page to fetch never run it: text imports (POST /api/import/text, which start at extract_recipe from the job's source_text output), photo imports, and paprika/raw-recipe imports (which start at parse_ingredients). \
The status API (server/src/scraping/status.rs build_step_states) then reports fetch_html as \"pending\" even after the job completes, so the web /scrape/:id page and the iOS text-import progress list show a step that looks stuck. \
Fix on the server: either leave fetch_html out of the plan for a job that has no fetch_html output and doesn't start there, or report it as \"skipped\". \
Both clients render whatever steps the API returns, so no client change should be needed beyond checking the result. \
No pipeline data/ diffs expected.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
